{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>the fifth time</b><br>A bundle of myrrh. Some say that myrrh is the musk [in Arabic], and the word אריתי (I gathered) would corrupt this interpretation, for it is from precious spice, and the sense of צרור המור (bundle of myrrh) is like צרור הכסף (bundle of silver)." "<b>the third time</b><br>Shaddai. These are the teachings and commandments that he would teach to the people of his generation, [until they acknowledged that there is none like HaShem, blessed be He], just as no cluster like that of Ein Gedi is found, which declares the praise of HaShem."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:53.764630919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}